2026-11-13T00:30:54.0951760Z #!/usr/bin/env python3
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0952121Z """Classify how a core-lane run actually died, from the GitHub REST job record.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0952439Z 
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0952614Z Why this module exists (operational resume of run 39082232157)
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0952998Z --------------------------------------------------------------
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0953432Z The product lane's own history now contains several DISTINCT death classes, and
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0953844Z conflating them has repeatedly cost cycles:
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0954046Z 
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0954319Z * ``rc 78 LEX_WORK_QUANTUM_EXPIRED`` — the wrapper killed the agent at 2700 s.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0954812Z   That is a *failure*, it is recorded in the job logs, and the snapshot survives.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0955380Z * misplaced gate file / lowercase ``_gate.json`` — the audit *agent* finished and
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0956034Z   the workflow's own reader step died.  Also a *failure*.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0956886Z * provider auth/overload — the agent step exits non-zero; also a *failure*.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0957444Z * **audit-step cancellation** (this module's subject) — the run concludes
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0957929Z   ``cancelled``; steps 6/7 are ``skipped``; NO audit branch exists; the lane is
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0958429Z   re-dispatched by the resilience job.  None of the above words describe it.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0958721Z 
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0958911Z For run 39082232157 the observed record was: ``team`` success in 18 m 56 s
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0959402Z (snapshot ``68bdae8`` persisted on ``cycle/core/product/39082232157/team``), then
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0959904Z the audit job's ``Independent audit`` step running 54 m 59 s and concluding
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0960397Z ``cancelled`` at 2026-10-18T01:33:15Z.  There is no ``.../audit`` branch on the
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0960808Z remote, so the work is *unaudited*, not rejected.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0961022Z 
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0961230Z ``.github/** is control-plane scope and is never edited from this lane.  So this
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0961709Z module does not patch the workflow; it makes the observed class **machine
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0962174Z checkable** so the next dispatch, report and auditor all read the same fact
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0962559Z instead of re-deriving it from prose.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0962736Z 
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0962813Z Design notes
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0962993Z ------------
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0963267Z * REUSE: the HTTP layer, ``observe_run`` and ``observe_jobs`` come from
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0963694Z   :mod:`product.ci_run_evidence` rather than being re-implemented.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0964146Z * The classifier is a **pure function** of a job record, so it is unit-testable
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0964764Z   with no network.  Only :func:`observe_steps` touches the network.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0965220Z * A run whose records cannot be fetched is reported as ``UNOBSERVABLE`` and is
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0965714Z   never silently treated as success, failure or cancellation.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0966503Z * Classification is a *set* of predicates over the record, and the evidence for
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0966993Z   each fired predicate is published, so a reader can disagree with the label by
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0967375Z   reading the same numbers.
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0967525Z 
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0967595Z Usage
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0967762Z -----
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0968061Z     python product/orchestration_evidence.py --run-id 39082232157 --write
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0968558Z     python product/orchestration_evidence.py --run-id 39082232157        # dry run
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0968935Z """
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0969125Z from __future__ import annotations
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0969293Z 
2026-11-13T00:30:54.0969379Z import argparse
