2026-11-13T00:39:29.7387473Z #!/usr/bin/env python3
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7388012Z """Bounded audit-readiness dossier for a resumed product snapshot.
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7388467Z 
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7388607Z Why this exists
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7388918Z ---------------
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7389406Z Run 40196023042's producer finished cleanly and persisted a real delta, but its
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7389957Z independent audit died at ``LEX_WORK_QUANTUM_EXPIRED seconds=2700`` (exit 78)
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7390475Z before writing a gate.  The next auditor should not have to spend its own
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7391028Z quantum rediscovering the slice, the accepted pointer or which artifacts are
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7391590Z claim-bearing.  This module gives it one command that re-derives the snapshot's
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7392327Z claims on bounded inputs and records the exact evidence.
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7392581Z 
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7392668Z What it does
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7392864Z ------------
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7393101Z * runs the product-owned state contract;
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7393486Z * checks the fail-closed posture and the accepted pointer;
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7393959Z * re-classifies the resumed run from its committed run/jobs snapshot;
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7394486Z * verifies the resumed run's committed diagnosis (quantum expiry, durable
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7394911Z   delta, unadjudicated status);
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7395313Z * hashes and structurally checks the claim-bearing artifacts (including the
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7395803Z   before/after bytes for the v68 rejection/incumbent leg);
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7396750Z * re-runs the shipped progressive query smoke over a real socket in fixture
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7397200Z   mode (no network, no paid inference);
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7397517Z * runs the bounded MVP core pytest set;
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7397935Z * confirms the producer wrote no auditor-namespace path and minted no gate.
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7398275Z 
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7398511Z It deliberately does NOT write ``results/audit/**``, mint a gate, score a
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7399051Z frozen bar, re-run a serve verdict, or label any run accepted/rejected.  Its
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7399562Z output is a dossier for the independent auditor, never a verdict.
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7399850Z 
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7399935Z Usage
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7400121Z -----
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7400397Z     python3 product/audit_readiness.py --run-id 40200882831 \\
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7400909Z         --out results/product/audit_readiness/CYCLE_40200882831_audit_readiness.json
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7401277Z 
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7401436Z     # fast mode while iterating (skip the two slow re-runs):
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7402139Z     python3 product/audit_readiness.py --run-id X --skip-tests --skip-smoke --out /tmp/x.json
2026-11-13T00:39:29.7402642Z """
