2026-11-13T00:48:02.7277836Z # The dossier was originally pinned to one snapshot (40196023042, resumed by
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7278669Z # 40200882831).  Every later operational resume needs the same bounded
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7279480Z # dossier, so the run-specific facts live in profiles instead of being
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7280028Z # re-derived per cycle.  A profile is selected by the --run-id argument
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7280484Z # (either the resuming run or the resumed snapshot) and falls back to
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7280953Z # ``DEFAULT_PROFILE_KEY`` so the original pinned behaviour is unchanged.
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7281435Z # Everything a profile does NOT override (posture, accepted pointer, frozen
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7281915Z # claim artifacts, MVP test set) is shared by design: those are accepted
2026-11-13T00:48:02.7282292Z # evidence, not per-run facts.
