2026-11-13T00:48:03.3625640Z """Product-owned reproduction of the core-lane orchestration contract.
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3625934Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3626029Z Why this module exists
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3626513Z ----------------------
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3626853Z The v50 lane was interrupted twice by the *same* defect and the repair never
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3627238Z held:
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3627338Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3627623Z * run 38548957828 — ``Validate active MVP producer state`` died because
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3628121Z   ``state/product.json`` still carried ``direction_version`` 48 while the run
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3628505Z   was dispatched with 49.
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3628904Z * run 38648548635 — the same step died again: the canonical file was still at
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3629401Z   ``direction_version`` 50 while the run was dispatched with 51, because the
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3629907Z   producer wrote a *shadow* copy at ``product/state/product.json`` (which is in
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3630400Z   lane write scope, so the shell scope check never saw it) instead of the
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3630794Z   workflow-validated ``state/product.json``.
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3631147Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3631376Z Shell ``case`` globs cannot express "this file is inside the scope prefix but is
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3631905Z not the file the workflow reads". This module is the product's own executable
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3632387Z copy of the contract, so a cycle can fail its own test in seconds instead of
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3632832Z burning a 45-minute workflow quantum to learn the same thing.
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3633082Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3633213Z What is reproduced (no gate logic is invented here)
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3633528Z ---------------------------------------------------
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3633989Z 1. ``Validate active MVP producer state`` — ``.github/workflows/core-lane.yml``
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3634428Z    runs ``jq -e '(.direction_version // -1) == $dirv and
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3634844Z    (.cycle_status // "INITIALIZED") != "INITIALIZED"' state/product.json`` and
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3635243Z    exits 68 (missing file) or 69 (assertion false).
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3635696Z 2. ``Enforce lane write scope`` — the same workflow rejects any pending path
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3636388Z    outside ``product/``, ``tests/product/``, ``results/product/``,
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3636814Z    ``reports/product/``, ``state/product.json`` and ``data/product/``.
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3637237Z 3. The audit-artifact contract: ``results/audit/<lane>/`` and
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3637657Z    ``reports/audit/<lane>/`` belong to the *independent auditor* only. A
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3638112Z    producer run that writes a ``CYCLE_<run>_GATE.json`` is self-minting an
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3638596Z    audit verdict, which is a forbidden fabrication even though the path never
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3638978Z    reaches the gate reader.
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3639127Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3639200Z Usage
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3639369Z -----
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3639646Z     python product/state_contract.py --check --direction-version 51
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3640116Z     python product/state_contract.py --check --direction-version 51 --scope
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3640627Z     python product/state_contract.py --check --direction-version 51 --git-status
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3641146Z """
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3641336Z from __future__ import annotations
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3641508Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3641595Z import argparse
2026-11-13T00:48:03.3641789Z import json
