2026-11-13T00:48:40.8383553Z results/product/orchestration/CYCLE_40193974025_team_step_raw.json \ --out
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8384375Z results/product/orchestration/CYCLE_40193974025_resume_diagnosis.json When no
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8385244Z public run/jobs snapshot was captured for the resumed run (for example an
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8386327Z operational resume dispatched straight from a failed run whose logs are not
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8386886Z reachable from the producer environment), omit ``--raw``: the instrument then
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8387377Z records ``RAW_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE`` / ``mechanism_unobserved`` instead of
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8387861Z inventing a cause, while still proving the durable-delta fact from git refs.
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8388358Z ``--predecessor-ref`` (default ``origin/lab/product``) compares the snapshot
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8388841Z against the accepted head the failed run was dispatched from, which is the
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8389324Z right delta baseline for a resume run: comparing against the previous *team*
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8389817Z ref would count the accepted audit commit as if the failed run had produced
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8390296Z it. Refs must already be available locally (the workflow fetches ``main``,
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8391033Z ``lab/<lane>`` and the team ref). The instrument never fetches, so an offline
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8391517Z reproduction is honest about a missing ref instead of silently reaching the
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8391897Z network.
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8392004Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8392081Z options:
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8392323Z   -h, --help            show this help message and exit
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8392630Z   --run-id RUN_ID
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8392870Z   --predecessor-run-id PREDECESSOR_RUN_ID
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8393191Z                         previous cycle's team ref (optional when
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8393529Z                         --predecessor-ref is given)
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8393826Z   --predecessor-ref PREDECESSOR_REF
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8394138Z                         explicit git ref for the durable-delta baseline
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8394489Z                         (default origin/lab/product)
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8394853Z   --raw RAW             committed run/jobs snapshot for --run-id; omit when
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8395305Z                         unavailable
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8395703Z   --out OUT
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8395975Z ====
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8396478Z usage: audit_step_diagnosis.py [-h] --raw RAW --out OUT
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8396708Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8396912Z Classify why a core-lane run stopped before an independent audit gate. Why
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8397603Z this exists --------------- The product cycle is routinely resumed with the
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8398477Z instruction "diagnose the orchestration/validation failure". From the producer
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8399385Z tree alone the important facts are: did the team job persist its snapshot, did
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8400254Z the provider/agent step fail, and did an independent gate ever get written?
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8401125Z This module answers those questions from a committed GitHub Actions run/jobs
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8401958Z snapshot -- no token, no job logs, no guessing at a cause it cannot observe.
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8402588Z It deliberately does NOT: * claim a provider/auth/quantum mechanism when the
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8403464Z log is unavailable; * treat a failed audit *or team* job as a product defect
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8404652Z or as a verdict; * write ``results/audit/**`` (only the independent auditor
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8405372Z may write there). The ``team`` block reports the persist step's OWN
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8406328Z conclusion. This matters because the workflow guards that step with ``if:
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8407148Z always()``: a failed producer still publishes its (possibly unchanged) tree to
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8407976Z the team ref, so "team job failed" must never be reported as "no snapshot
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8408502Z exists". Whether that snapshot carries a durable delta is a separate, git-ref
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8408981Z fact and is deliberately not inferred here. Usage ----- python3
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8409438Z product/audit_step_diagnosis.py --raw <snapshot.json> --out <dir>
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8409713Z 
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8409815Z options:
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8410218Z   -h, --help  show this help message and exit
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8410719Z   --raw RAW   committed run/jobs snapshot
2026-11-13T00:48:40.8411190Z   --out OUT   output JSON path
